Z||000000||JJ-85-2M6||11-17-2001||09:00 AM||||Re: the earlier post...Is there supposed to be a gap between the headliner board and the edges of the roof.  I have that with my car too, and it is the original headliner as far as I know. I haven't recovered it myself, because of this 1-2 inch gap in some places. You can feel that there is nothing there but fabric...Anyone know about this??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-17-2001||02:43 PM||||I never had that problem with my original headliner.  Just with the FS fiberglass unit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JJ-85-2M6||11-19-2001||08:11 PM||||Maybe its a replacement.  Anyway, I looked at it again and realized the gaps are around the sunroof opening on all 4 sides!  J||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-19-2001||08:25 PM||||I just went out and checked mine ('88 w/sunroof).  <P>I bought the car from the original dealer and ordered from the factory.  It is original STOCK!!  <P>There IS a gap all 'round every edge.  As best I can feel, it seems about 1/4 to 1/2 inch everywhere (including the overhead console) - I hadn't noticed that before today!  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||11-19-2001||09:43 PM||||There is a gap but when the headliner material is tucked into the sunroof channel and the trim molding applied it is not visible. There also will be a gap across the front of the windshield. Headliners seem to fit well up to the roof line in the rear though.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
